2. Permissions

You may view and study the publicly available source, download and run an
unmodified official release for personal use, and make private backup or test
copies. You may modify a private copy for your own use. You may fork the
repository solely to prepare and submit a contribution to the official
MostLight repository. Keep copyright and license notices in these copies.

You may include and redistribute an official, unmodified MostLight JAR in a
Minecraft modpack or launcher, including a publicly distributed modpack,
provided that you:

  (a) obtain the JAR from an official NokhXyr release and do not modify,
      recompile, or repackage it;
  (b) preserve its copyright and license notices and identify NokhXyr as the
      author, with a link to the official repository in the pack's mod list or
      documentation where such a list exists; and
  (c) do not sell or paywall MostLight as a separate product, or present the
      mod as your own work.

The modpack or launcher may be distributed free of charge or as part of a
monetized offering, but this permission does not grant rights over Minecraft,
NeoForge, or any other included mod or asset. You are responsible for their
separate license terms.

Builds, screenshots and videos made in game with the Mod, including servers,
maps and creations that use its blocks, are yours to share.

3. Restrictions

Except for the modpack and launcher permission in Section 2, without prior
written permission from NokhXyr, you may not publish, redistribute, mirror,
sell, sublicense, or rebrand the Mod or a modified build; use its original
source code, models, textures or other assets in another project; or remove
authorship and license notices. Linking to the official repository or
official release is allowed. Public repository visibility does not grant
open-source rights.

4. Contributions

By submitting code, assets, translations, or documentation for inclusion in
MostLight, you confirm that you have the right to submit them and grant
